{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_6e1053ae16b0588144d67f731748942a1c66c825b4ef3ddd148115d684446aa9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is positioned as a Langchain agent creator aimed at helping developers, researchers, and AI enthusiasts build, prototype, and deploy AI-powered agents."},{"claim_ids":["clm_74317eae5709bcbc0566812c8c9a364a9dbd50506f95d50e10523a888a0f54a9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool supports creating and testing agents and tools on the fly, enabling rapid prototyping without lengthy setup."},{"claim_ids":["clm_82e3ed4d71727c1ba3cd72c3607bb1f8f71a412fab0b1d39fbb6c3cd7512fbde"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README encourages contributions and references a CONTRIBUTING guide for submission guidelines."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a1f7741271e955105ffde4c9c2b37ffced4d02f34d67c2611adedf382a50d490"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product advertises session-persistent memory that preserves user work across multiple sessions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a2d50d081a9e1e2380e36c71ca7123331022f161349ac3c37011805fd2b6d882"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Detailed documentation covering use cases, tools, agents, toolkits, and agent executors is hosted at an external GitBook docs site."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a8e11bb890dd14a3f1ac516ff1c17a7af0953b4712d4b73dae0de128afd5f57e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product provides an interactive command-line interface with real-time feedback for navigating, managing, and executing commands."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c62b62a4b17ba0049a5862d2ee5eed124f33d4f6c4f7485228ecc94f50de802c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool is invoked from the terminal by typing the command 'yeagerai-agent', after which users can build agents on the fly."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c7d9538ec100a48f5a38d9b147674450018b0840f9e6960973ca35129608dd86"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states the project is discontinued, and points readers to a successor repository, genlayerlabs/subzeroclaw."},{"cl